 #   ghcr.io/xarmian/algod-rust:<tag>-localnet   — `localnet` target (single
 #                                                  node dev-mode network)
 #
+# The same two images are **also** mirrored to Docker Hub, at
+# `docker.io/<DOCKERHUB_USERNAME>/algod-rust[:<tag>[-localnet]]` — same
+# tags, same digests (built once, pushed to both registries) — but only if
+# the `DOCKERHUB_USERNAME` and `DOCKERHUB_TOKEN` repository secrets are
+# configured. Without them, every Docker Hub step is skipped automatically
+# and only GHCR is published (this is the default state for a fresh fork).
+# See docs/DOCKER_CI.md for exactly what to set up and why.
+#
 # ## Pipeline shape
 #
 # `prepare` computes the release channel (nightly / stable / beta / plain
-# main build) and shared tag inputs once. `build` then builds+pushes each
-# (target x platform) image **by digest only, one platform per job, on that
-# platform's own native runner** (`ubuntu-24.04-arm` for arm64) — no QEMU
-# emulation, which previously made multi-arch `main`-branch pushes exceed
-# the job timeout entirely (see git history / issue tracker: both push-to-
-# main builds since this workflow's introduction were killed at 45min).
-# `merge` then combines each target's two per-platform digests into one
-# multi-arch manifest list and applies the real tag set from `prepare`.
-# `pr-check` replaces all of the above on pull_request: a single amd64,
-# no-push build per target, just to catch a broken Dockerfile before merge.
+# main build), shared tag inputs, and whether Docker Hub is configured,
+# once. `build` then builds+pushes each (target x platform) image **by
+# digest only, one platform per job, on that platform's own native runner**
+# (`ubuntu-24.04-arm` for arm64) — no QEMU emulation, which previously made
+# multi-arch `main`-branch pushes exceed the job timeout entirely (see git
+# history / issue tracker: both push-to-main builds since this workflow's
+# introduction were killed at 45min) — pushing by digest to GHCR and (if
+# configured) Docker Hub in the same build. `merge` then combines each
+# target's two per-platform digests into one multi-arch manifest list per
+# registry and applies the real tag set from `prepare`. `pr-check` replaces
+# all of the above on pull_request: a single amd64, no-push build per
+# target, just to catch a broken Dockerfile before merge.
 #
 # ## Triggers
 #
